% review-findings: No words in the file. The zashiki-asobi it belongs to is traditionally a drinking game at geisha parties in Kotohira: the player who hesitates drinks.
% review-suggestion: Keep the tune and the hand game; reword the dossier from "party game" to "a party hand game from Kotohira" and teach the touching game only.
% review-decision: published to main on 11 November 2026 as the melody without words (none in the transcription), with the touching game only, described as a party hand game from Kotohira and nothing said of drinking; keep correcting here (words still to add, notes still to check against Nagai and Obata 1895)
