R:zashiki game song
S:Nagai Iwai and Obata Kenhachiro (eds.), 1895, via Daisyfield.com transcription (Tom Potter, 2008, donated to the public domain)
N:The game: two players face each other across a small stand and touch it in turn, in time to the song, which goes faster each time round. The ending is on G with the yo scale's G A C D E, so the band holds G and D (an open fifth, written G5) rather than changing chords. No words in the source file.
